---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import '../../styles/homelab.css';
---

<Layout>
  <main class="homelab-page">

    <section class="homelab-hero">
      <div class="homelab-heading">
        <a class="back-link" href="/projects">← Projects</a>

        <p class="homelab-label">
          02 · Linux · Networking · Self-hosting
        </p>

        <h1 class="homelab-title">Homelab</h1>

        <p class="homelab-intro">
          What started as a home server has grown into a homelab where I run
          the services I use at home and learn as I build, maintain and troubleshoot it.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="homelab-meta">
        <div>
          <span>Platform</span>
          <strong>Ubuntu Linux</strong>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>Infrastructure</span>
          <strong>Docker · UniFi</strong>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>Focus</span>
          <strong>Networking · Automation · Self-hosting</strong>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>


    <section class="story-section">
      <div class="story-heading">
        <span>Overview</span>

        <h2>
          My server.<br />
          My home network.
        </h2>
      </div>

      <div class="story-copy">
        <p>
          Today, the homelab consists of an Ubuntu server running most of my services in
          Docker, alongside a UniFi-managed network and Home Assistant for home
          automation.
        </p>

        <p>
          Because I use it every day, it has also become a practical place to learn.
          When something breaks, I have to work out whether the problem is in
          a container, the host, DNS or the network.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>


    <section class="network-section">
      <div class="network-heading">
        <span>Architecture</span>

        <h2>
          How the network<br />
          is arranged.
        </h2>

        <p>
          UniFi handles routing, firewall rules and network segmentation.
          The Ubuntu server runs most of my self-hosted services.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="network-map" aria-label="Simplified homelab architecture">

        <div class="network-tier">
          <div class="network-tier-label">
            <span>01</span>
            Edge
          </div>

          <div class="network-node network-node-main">
            <span class="node-type">WAN</span>
            <strong>Internet</strong>
            <small>Internet connection</small>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="network-link" aria-hidden="true">
          <span></span>
        </div>

        <div class="network-tier">
          <div class="network-tier-label">
            <span>02</span>
            Network
          </div>

          <div class="network-node network-node-accent">
            <span class="node-type">GATEWAY</span>
            <strong>UniFi</strong>
            <small>Routing · firewall · segmentation</small>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="network-link" aria-hidden="true">
          <span></span>
        </div>

        <div class="network-tier">
          <div class="network-tier-label">
            <span>03</span>
            Segments
          </div>

          <div class="network-branches">
            <div class="network-node">
              <span class="node-type">LAN</span>
              <strong>Trusted devices</strong>
              <small>Workstations · server</small>
            </div>

            <div class="network-node">
              <span class="node-type">VLAN</span>
              <strong>IoT</strong>
              <small>Separated smart devices</small>
            </div>

            <div class="network-node">
              <span class="node-type">VPN</span>
              <strong>Remote access</strong>
              <small>VPN access from outside</small>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="network-link" aria-hidden="true">
          <span></span>
        </div>

        <div class="network-tier">
          <div class="network-tier-label">
            <span>04</span>
            Compute
          </div>

          <div class="network-node network-node-server">
            <span class="node-type">LINUX</span>
            <strong>Ubuntu server</strong>
            <small>Docker · storage · automation</small>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="network-link" aria-hidden="true">
          <span></span>
        </div>

        <div class="network-tier">
          <div class="network-tier-label">
            <span>05</span>
            Services
          </div>

          <div class="service-grid">
            <div>DNS</div>
            <div>Automation</div>
            <div>Media</div>
            <div>Monitoring</div>
            <div>Web hosting</div>
            <div>Reverse proxy</div>
          </div>
        </div>

      </div>
    </section>


    <section class="principles-section">
      <div class="principles-heading">
        <span>Approach</span>

        <h2>
          How I run<br />
          the homelab.
        </h2>
      </div>

      <div class="principles-grid">

        <article class="principle">
          <span>01</span>
          <h3>Keep it local</h3>
          <p>
            I prefer running services locally when it makes
            sense, especially for home automation and services I rely on at home.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="principle">
          <span>02</span>
          <h3>Segment deliberately</h3>
          <p>
            I keep IoT devices separate from trusted systems and use firewall
            rules to allow only the traffic they actually need.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="principle">
          <span>03</span>
          <h3>Understand what breaks</h3>
          <p>
            When something fails, I want to understand where and why rather
            than simply getting it working again.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="principle">
          <span>04</span>
          <h3>Keep it maintainable</h3>
          <p>
            I organise services into Docker Compose stacks to keep configuration,
            updates and changes manageable.
          </p>
        </article>

      </div>
    </section>


    <section class="stack-section">
      <div class="stack-heading">
        <span>Stack</span>

        <h2>
          What I use at home.
        </h2>
      </div>

      <div class="stack-list">
        <div>
          <span>Operating system</span>
          <strong>Ubuntu Linux</strong>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>Containers</span>
          <strong>Docker · Docker Compose</strong>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>Networking</span>
          <strong>UniFi · VLANs · Firewalls</strong>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>DNS</span>
          <strong>Pi-hole</strong>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>Remote access</span>
          <strong>WireGuard · Teleport</strong>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>Automation</span>
          <strong>Home Assistant · ESPHome</strong>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>Web</span>
          <strong>Caddy · HTTPS · Astro</strong>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>Administration</span>
          <strong>SSH · UFW · Fail2Ban</strong>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>


    <section class="homelab-closing">
      <div class="closing-heading">
        <span>Ongoing project</span>

        <h2>
          Built to be used.<br />
          Never really finished.
        </h2>
      </div>

      <div class="closing-content">
        <p>
          The homelab changes as I find new things I want to run, improve or
          understand. I document the setup as it evolves, both for my own reference
          and to keep track of how and why things are configured.
        </p>

        <a
          class="github-link"
          href="https://github.com/Pdoxxy/homelab-infrastructure"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noreferrer"
        >
          View infrastructure documentation on GitHub
          <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>

  </main>
</Layout>
